# Reference-only control file: scripts/package.sh (fpm-based) is the
# actual build/package path used by CI (release.yml, install-test.yml)
# and documented in scripts/package.sh's own header -- it emits a
# single generic fractalsql-mariadb_<version>_<arch>.deb, not a
# per-major package, since the UDF ABI is stable across MariaDB
# 10.6/10.11/11.4 LTS/12.3 LTS. There is no debian/rules or
# debian/*.install here, so this file alone does not build a package;
# it exists so the dependency/description metadata for a future native
# dpkg-buildpackage flow doesn't drift from what fpm actually ships
# (both fractalsql.so, the GPL-2.0-only shim, and fractalsqld, the
# Apache-2.0 daemon -- never just the shim, since nothing would run the
# UDF bodies the shim forwards calls to). See debian-copyright
# (one level up) for the per-file license breakdown.
Package: fractalsql-mariadb
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 libc6 (>= 2.34),
 libcurl4,
 libssl3,
 mariadb-server
Description: Stochastic Fractal Search UDF for MariaDB, plus its daemon
 fractalsql-mariadb registers the fractal_search() UDF, a Stochastic
 Fractal Search optimizer that returns JSON top-k matches for a query
 vector against an inline corpus, plus the full Discovery/Vector/
 Cognition/Text-to-SQL/Agency/Enterprise-activation tier surface (see
 docs/features.md). Pure-C vendored core, no LuaJIT runtime
 dependency. Compatible with MariaDB 10.6 / 10.11 / 11.4 LTS / 12.3
 LTS -- the UDF ABI has been stable across these majors.
 .
 mariadbd loads only a thin shim (fractalsql.so); every UDF body runs
 in the separate fractalsqld daemon this package also installs and
 runs via systemd (fractalsqld.service). The bundled
 fractalsql-reasoning-http.so plugin (Cognition/Text-to-SQL/
 Vectorizer/Agency tiers), loaded by the daemon, dynamically links
 libcurl at runtime, hence the libcurl4 dependency above. libssl3 is
 for the daemon's enterprise-library signature check; the shim links
 no OpenSSL.
